{"skill":{"slug":"link-skill","displayName":"LinkSKILL"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1778688286474,"changelog":"- Initial release of link-skill as version 1.0.1.\n- Added core modules: `auth_manager.py` (authentication), `http_request_tool.py` (API request execution), and `swagger_loader.py` (OpenAPI/Swagger discovery).\n- Introduced config-driven platform selection and authentication management.\n- Supports API exploration, search, detail inspection, and standard request execution via CLI.\n- Local caching for tokens and swagger schemas to improve repeated workflows.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"scripts/auth_manager.py","size":5255,"sha256":"d3c90eafd742f3ff963d32943e4c0f1c3c662c26a1c977ece312388f2dad74d8","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/http_request_tool.py","size":5004,"sha256":"f703b0f61bb1c66e95856afdc63a0c37679cb477c5cea40ac16e4696c3258bb9","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/swagger_loader.py","size":11391,"sha256":"b19e9219485fb1ad3bd04f13dd3547bc74ddc67a41e0c489670ce08395c611df","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5005,"sha256":"53a0c49e4e8363c8b0d52fabd1b10e860b57de3f135be9449783bb95d12ef440","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2289,"sha256":"7d9acc95f720e4264cab4206b9082d0bb4110c7e1b139b28997afd09455274f1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789195493659,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8f67f8ebc0209fd4feca7e278b9ed8387e6f5b900155b1473b91c79009cbd314","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8f67f8ebc0209fd4feca7e278b9ed8387e6f5b900155b1473b91c79009cbd314","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090800423},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":14,"checkedAt":1789195493659},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a plausible API integration helper, but it handles reusable credentials unsafely and can attach them to arbitrary HTTP requests.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access and local file reads/writes are coherent for this purpose, but forwarding cached auth headers to any supplied --url is overbroad for an enterprise integration tool.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains a skill document and Python helper scripts with metadata requiring python3 and the requests package; no hidden installer, startup hook, service, or dependency confusion pattern was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill describes broad 'universal' use for any platform and documents token caching and request execution, but it lacks clear safety boundaries, destination restrictions, destructive-action confirmation, or warnings about credential exposure.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persists bearer/API/basic credentials in scripts/.token_cache.json without enforced restrictive permissions and prints full cached tokens through normal and diagnostic code paths; no system-level persistence was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Swagger/OpenAPI discovery, authentication, and request execution, which matches the included scripts, but the request tool supports full URLs plus POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE while automatically injecting cached credentials.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only after reviewing and preferably fixing credential handling. Use non-production credentials, avoid --url with a configured authenticated platform, avoid --show-cache, rotate any token printed in logs, and restrict use to trusted endpoints until destination allowlisting, redaction, file-permission hardening, and destructive-request confirmation are added.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Authenticated request execution and automatic re-authentication are documented and purpose-aligned, but the unrestricted destination and destructive method support make the authority under-scoped rather than malicious.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact-backed code prints complete cached tokens and dumps the full token cache with --show-cache, which is not necessary for the stated workflow and creates a real credential-disclosure concern.\n[SQP-2] expected: A local token cache is disclosed and coherent with repeatable API calls, but storing reusable credentials as plaintext JSON without permission hardening is a material handling concern.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: http_request_tool.py loads a configured platform token and can send it to an arbitrary --url rather than only the configured gateway, so the scanner's credential-forwarding concern is supported by the artifact.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill does not declare tight permission boundaries for shell, network, or file access despite handling credentials and arbitrary API requests.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The 'universal' and 'any platform' framing is broader than the implemented safety controls and may encourage use with sensitive systems without adequate scoping.\n[E1] expected: The login POST is to the configured platform gateway and is expected for authentication; I did not find a hardcoded exfiltration destination.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The stdout exposure of full cached authentication material is directly present in auth_manager.py and is not required for normal operation.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The --show-cache help text sounds like inspection, but the implementation prints complete credential cache contents without redaction.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess use invokes the bundled auth_manager.py with an explicit argument list and shell=False; this supports auto re-authentication and does not by itself show command injection.\n[AST7] expected: Dynamic request dispatch is constrained by argparse HTTP-method choices, so this is a low-context coding pattern rather than an independent security concern.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan's core concerns are supported: cached credentials can be exposed through stdout, stored insecurely, and forwarded cross-origin when --url is used with a configured platform.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789195493659}}}}}